FTXUI 7.0.3 writes the whole screen on every frame and reads input 128 bytes at
a time, so one key costs ~3 KiB on the terminal and queued keys need many frames.
App has no output hook, so noteapp (T75) adds the smallest one:
- App::SetFrameWriter: noteapp's src/tui/frame_diff.cpp writes changed cells only.
- FetchTerminalEvents: 4096-byte read, all queued input lands in one frame.
FTXUI 7.0.3 has no bracketed paste either: a terminal paste came as key events,
CR LF as two Return events (an extra blank line per line). noteapp (NY-T) adds:
- Install: DECSET 2004 (bracketed paste), reset on Uninstall.
- TerminalInputParser: ESC[200~ text ESC[201~ is one Event::Special whose input
  is "\x1B[200~" + the raw text (no CR -> LF uniformization); outside a paste,
  CR LF within the 50 ms key timeout is one Return.
- App::SetPasteTimeout: a paste with no input for that long ends as if
  ESC[201~ came (a lost end mark must not swallow every key); 0 = never.
  Bytes that come after that are the rest of the paste, delivered as one more
  paste event at ESC[201~ or after one more silent timeout, never as keys.
- App::SetPasteLimit: bytes past the limit are not kept; the paste ends as
  Event::Special("\x1B[noteapp-paste-too-large"). Event::SpecialOwned moves
  the kept bytes into the event: no copy on the parser -> event queue path.
  App still hands the Event by value to ComponentBase::OnEvent (a copy per
  layer, as for any event). The limit counts the end mark too: a paste that
  times out without it may carry up to 6 bytes more (the app checks again).
Drop this patch when upstream offers an output hook and bracketed paste;
re-check at every FTXUI bump. cmake/Dependencies.cmake refetches FTXUI when
this file changes (FetchContent alone would keep the old patched sources).

